Question:Which of the following statements about the role of the intestine in development of obesity best describes the situation?
Options:
A) Obesity occurs because gut hormone secretion becomes deranged and PYY secretion fails to give a satiety signal.
B) The gut/brain signalling pathway controls energy intake to within 2% of requirements, even in people who are morbidly obese
C) The problem is one of greed and gluttony, whereby people override strong satiety signals on a regular basis
D) Flavour signals from tasty, processed food will override satiety signals even after a large meal
Thought:
The intestine plays a key role in obesity through gut hormone regulation. PYY and other hormones signal satiety. If PYY secretion is impaired, satiety signals are reduced, leading to overeating. Option A directly addresses this mechanism. Other options either focus on psychological factors (C), overly precise physiological control (B), or flavor override (D) which is less central to the intestinal role in obesity development.
Ground truth: B
Answer: A
