Question:A blood sample is taken from a 45 year old man after he has broken his overnight fast by eating three slices of toast and a boiled egg. Which one of the following will be at a higher concentration than if the blood sample had been taken before breakfast?
Options:
A) Alanine
B) Glucose
C) Ketone bodies
D) Non-esterified (free) fatty acids
Thought:
After an overnight fast, the body relies on glycogen stores for glucose. Consuming carbohydrates (toast) and protein (egg) post-fast would increase glucose levels. Ketone bodies and free fatty acids decrease with food intake, while alanine levels may not show significant change. Thus, glucose concentration will be higher post-meal.
Ground truth: B
Answer: B
